  "body": "See https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#action-versus-occurance for why this is obsolete\n\nMost of the cases are \"has no default action\" which can just be removed. Some of them are integrated with cancelation and need a bit more care, e.g.\n\n> If the event's default action is prevented (i.e. if the event is canceled) then abort these steps.\n\nshould just become\n\n> If the event is canceled\n\nSome of the stuff around contextmenu seems more complicated as it's actually using default action. Similarly click.\n\nI don't think this is a good first bug.\n\nThis is partially covered by https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=12230. Maybe the thing to do is use this issue as a way to remove all the trivial uses and then create a checklist of the nontrivial uses.\n\nAssigning to @annevk as our DOM person.\n",
